  {
   "id": "verb-map",
   "level": "A2",
   "el": "Ο χάρτης του ρήματος",
   "title": "The verb map",
   "group": "verbs",
   "body": [
    {
     "p": "Every Greek verb has two stems: **imperfective** (ongoing, repeated: **γραφ-**) and **perfective** (single, complete: **γραψ-**). The tenses are combinations of a stem, a set of endings and the words **θα, να, έχω**."
    },
    {
     "table": {
      "head": [
       "",
       "Imperfective",
       "Perfective",
       "Perfect"
      ],
      "rows": [
       [
        "Non-past",
        "**γράφω** present",
        "(να) **γράψω** subjunctive",
        "**έχω γράψει**"
       ],
       [
        "Past",
        "**έγραφα** imperfect",
        "**έγραψα** aorist",
        "**είχα γράψει**"
       ],
       [
        "Future",
        "**θα γράφω**",
        "**θα γράψω**",
        "**θα έχω γράψει**"
       ],
       [
        "Imperative",
        "**γράφε, γράφετε**",
        "**γράψε, γράψτε**",
        ""
       ],
       [
        "Passive",
        "**γράφομαι, γραφόμουν**",
        "**γράφτηκα, (να) γραφτώ**",
        "**έχω γραφτεί**"
       ]
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "table": {
      "head": [
       "Participles",
       ""
      ],
      "rows": [
       [
        "gerund (active, invariable)",
        "**γράφοντας** \"writing, by writing\""
       ],
       [
        "passive perfect",
        "**γραμμένος, -η, -ο** \"written\""
       ]
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "list": [
      "**Know three forms** of each verb and you can build the rest: present **γράφω**, aorist **έγραψα**, passive aorist **γράφτηκα**.",
      "**θα + perfective** = simple future (\"I'll write\"); **θα + imperfective** = continuous or habitual future (\"I'll be writing, I'll write regularly\").",
      "**να + perfective / imperfective**: the subjunctive, used after θέλω, μπορώ, πρέπει, για να, πριν ..."
     ]
    },
    {
     "links": [
      {
       "href": "#b1-aspect",
       "kind": "Lesson",
       "el": "Ποιόν ενεργείας",
       "title": "Aspect: imperfective and perfective"
